cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "I-Lang Protocol Specification"
abstract: >-
  I-Lang is an AI-native communication protocol that defines a formal vocabulary
  of 88 verbs, 29 modifiers, 14 entities, and 13 Greek aliases for structured
  communication between humans and AI, between AI agents, and within AI internal
  reasoning. It introduces two syntaxes: operation syntax for executable
  instructions and declaration syntax for behavioral identity. v3.0 defines
  communication format, v4.0 adds execution semantics, and v5.0 adds a trainable
  judgment layer built on an 11-dimensional judgment vector space.
type: software
